| Existing support access | Up to six owner comparisons; O(m) rebuild or O(s) compaction; optional cache construction | Must not be hidden in a proposed sparse consumer |
| Direction validation and BFRT | Existing residual, finite and predicted-value scans; optional solves/refinement | All remain; this is not a complete backend work budget |

No production computational work, allocations, retained memory, cache,
precision, or safeguard changes were introduced. There is no new production
work or memory cost to justify and no benchmark requirement for this document.
Potential future support selection, scalar-object retention and fallback costs
are unresolved. No elapsed-time, allocation, native-free, or end-to-end claim
is made. Existing S3-A/B evidence is reused only for its original scope.

